{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794427166257463258,"compiled_state":{"alias":"idle-ammoniacal-axisdeer","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"947ea0a1b197b726fca50ccb525f1f229be3a9b05518850aa82c32a4ccb9fc17","event_uuid":"0c9f28a9-015a-4269-b7be-21b9105d6f83","position":{"commit_sha":"ec704d43ab1a2cda113a1d590efcce104166a39f","position":"1794427149318938547-0c9f28a9-015a-4269-b7be-21b9105d6f83"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"c32b3bac893b69675495d1b3b44da9f37e77a851eac616d2c61cf0330560e5b4","event_uuid":"99ad741a-3b03-4c30-afdc-a58305fb1c3b","position":{"commit_sha":"951bc6e6cd877ed4c6b2209d789a7660b7b068cf","position":"1794427166257463257-99ad741a-3b03-4c30-afdc-a58305fb1c3b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794427149318938547,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"99ad741a-3b03-4c30-afdc-a58305fb1c3b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"51e0-5038-bf00-4653"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`gitutil.run_git_bounded` runs git through `subprocess.run(..., timeout=...)`. When the bound expires, Python SIGKILLs only the direct `git` process. That causes two problems:\n\n- The git process cannot run its signal cleanup. `git fetch` registers a handler that removes its `objects/pack/pack-*.keep` file on signal, and SIGKILL bypasses it.\n- Children such as `index-pack` and `pack-objects` keep running after their parent dies. They are reparented to init, or to rebar-mcp when it is the container's PID 1.\n\nA `.keep` file excludes its pack from every later repack. Until someone deletes it by hand, that pack is never consolidated.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Production MCP tickets clone, inspected 2026-11-11. There were 12 `.keep` files, all reading `fetch-pack <pid> on <container-host>` and dated 2026-09-05 through 2026-09-15 UTC. No fetch was running. They were removed during the maintenance repair for bug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek`.\n- Local reproduction: a stand-in `git` that held a lock and had a child process was run through a `subprocess.run` timeout. The lock file stayed behind, and the child was reparented to PID 1. The same stand-in run under SIGTERM-first process-group reaping (`rebar._proc.reap_process_group`) cleaned up both.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nBug `nickelic-lazuline-gonolek` applied group reaping only to the explicit maintenance step. This ticket covers every other bounded git child: sync and push fetches and merges, and store commits.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] When a bounded git child times out, its whole process group is reaped, SIGTERM first, so no git descendant outlives the call.\n- [ ] A test proves that a bounded fetch interrupted by its bound leaves no `.keep` file and no surviving child process.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4eed-2e15-d018-4bd6","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bounded git timeout SIGKILLs only the parent, stranding fetch-pack .keep files and orphaning git children","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0c9f28a9-015a-4269-b7be-21b9105d6f83","99ad741a-3b03-4c30-afdc-a58305fb1c3b"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794427166257463258,"uuid":"e0d969e3-955c-4d31-bbab-65cfea5fe66f"}